    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44688" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sŏlūs</span></b> , untis,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σολοῦς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town on the northern
				coast of Sicily</i>, now <i>Castello di
			Solanto</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 8, 14, §
			90</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sŏ-luntīni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Solus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 43, § 103</span></i>;
				sing., <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 2,
			42</span></i>, § 102.</div>
